grep
Usage: grep [-HhnlLoqvsrRiwFE] [-m N] [-A|B|C N] { PATTERN | -e PATTERN... | -f FILE... } [FILE]...

Search for PATTERN in FILEs (or stdin).

	-H	Add 'filename:' prefix
	-h	Do not add 'filename:' prefix
	-n	Add 'line_no:' prefix
	-l	Names of matching files
	-L	Files with no match
	-c	Count matching lines
	-o	Only the matched text
	-q	Quiet, use exit status
	-v	Select non-matching lines
	-s	No error messages
	-r	Search subdirectories too
	-R	Recurse and dereference symlinks
	-i	Ignore case
	-w	Match whole words only
	-x	Match whole lines only
	-F	Plain text, not a regex
	-E	Extended regex, not basic
	-m N	Up to N matches per file
	-A N	N lines after each match
	-B N	N lines before each match
	-C N	Same as '-A N -B N'
	-e PATTERN	Pattern to match
	-f FILE	Read pattern from file
